# AI pipeline, reading and OCR

- Every model call goes through a provider protocol: `DeclarationExtractionProvider` in
  `backend/app/declarations/provider.py` for imports, `KnowledgeAnswerProvider` in
  `declarations/knowledge_provider.py` for property questions, `DocumentReadingProvider` in
  `declarations/provider.py` for reading a rendered page into a typed transcript with the organization's
  document reading model, `InvoiceExtractionProvider` in `declarations/provider.py` for the extraction stage of
  an unstructured invoice. Do not import the OpenAI SDK elsewhere.
- Reservation, usage and cost accounting live in `declarations/pipeline.py` (`add_usage`,
  `settle_reservation`, `charge_reservation`) with the per-run cap `declaration_max_cost_usd`;
  `core/runtime_budget.py` holds the QA policy checks. The pipeline fails closed when a cap or
  policy check fails. A per-organization budget is #22: keep the accounting attributable to the
  organization so it becomes possible.
- Tests use `declarations/fake_provider.py` and `fake_knowledge_provider.py` (and the offline worker
  `backend/tests/offline_declaration_import.py`); no live key, no network. Live evaluations are opt-in gates (`HV_DECLARATION_REAL_PDF_MANIFEST`,
  `HV_DECLARATION_RUNTIME_IMAGE`) and never run in CI.
- A change to prompts, schemas or the harness bumps the matching version: the settings
  `declaration_prompt_version`, `declaration_schema_version`, `declaration_harness_version`
  (`core/config.py`, defaults mirrored in `.env.example` and `docker-compose.prod.yml`) or the
  knowledge constants `KNOWLEDGE_QA_PROMPT_VERSION` and `KNOWLEDGE_ANSWER_SCHEMA_VERSION`; the reading and
  invoice stages version their own prompt and schema in constants (`READING_PROMPT_VERSION`,
  `READING_SCHEMA_VERSION`, `INVOICE_PROMPT_VERSION`, `INVOICE_SCHEMA_VERSION`), and a model-made
  invoice proposal carries `MODEL_PROCESSOR_VERSION` (`core/invoice_pdf.py`); extend
  `backend/tests/fixtures/declaration_eval_cases.json` for extraction changes. Evidence, review
  and approval records stay reproducible from stored inputs.
- Local text recognition is Tesseract (`deu`) with poppler and qpdf, run as bounded subprocesses (DPI,
  pixels, pages, temp bytes, timeout) in `core/invoice_ocr.py`, `core/pdf_extraction.py`,
  `core/visual_extract.py` and `core/intake_extraction.py`. A path that reads with a model renders its
  pages with poppler the same bounded way (`declarations/preflight.py`) and has no Tesseract step. Keep
  every new path bounded the same way.
- The invoice worker sends an unstructured PDF to the organization's models only when its AI import switch, key
  and models allow it (`ai_settings_service.invoice_import_blocker`); structured invoices never reach a model. Each
  request is reserved and settled in `invoice_model_call` (`declarations/invoice_pipeline.py`), outside any
  transaction, within the documented per-invoice bounds (constants there, not settings); the path has no
  Tesseract step. The confirmation text that names invoices governs transmission, so an organization that
  confirmed an older text keeps its invoices on the host until it confirms again. A retry reads and pays
  again: page transcripts of an invoice are not stored.
- A stage that calls a model meters it in the shared ledger by the model that made the call (reserve
  before, settle after, keep the usage of failed calls) and records it in the pass ledger with its
  `pass_id`; a view of per-stage usage reads that ledger and the run row in one aggregation
  (`api/declaration_imports.py`), never a second counter.
- Documents and extracted text leave the host only to the configured provider from a worker that
  has the provider network (the declaration worker; the invoice worker where Compose gives it the same
  `backend` and `egress` networks, never wider; `DEPLOY.md`); respect `HV_DATA_REGION`. Observability
  records (`declarations/observability.py`) and logs carry identifiers, versions, hashes and
  usage, never document text.
- The provider-neutral runtime (#66) uses the existing typed interfaces and deterministic
  manager; see ADR 0014. Model-based reading with two model roles replaces Tesseract path by path
  (#65, ADR 0017): a path that reads with a model has no Tesseract step or fallback, and there is no
  separate OCR service.
